            <div xml:id="d536">

                <pb facs="0667" n="523" sameAs="frus:frus1929v02/pg523"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/1160: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in China</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-01-31T11:00:00-05:00">January 31, 1929—11
                        a.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>42. Your 68, January 30, 7 p.m. I am in favor of the cancellation of the arms
                    embargo to China. The United States has to do that by a proclamation of the
                    President which he can make at any time. Wire me if the Diplomatic Body are
                    ready to cancel the agreement and I will have the President issue a
                    proclamation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
